          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In general, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacuum"} perturbative string theory vacuum
            is defined by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"}> 2-spectral triple
            ”) of the corresponding emergent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
          %p
            Some such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFTs"} 2d SCFTs
            arise as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            from actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} manifolds
            with differential geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+fields"} background fields
            on them. These are hence called the
            %em geometric vacua
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em geometric backgrounds
          %p
            All other vacua are then called
            = succeed "." do
              %em non-geometric backgrounds
            %em only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell-dually
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebra"} vertex operator algebra
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            of a non-geometric background is dually an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+of+a+vertex+operator+algebra"} automorphism of a vertex operator algebra
          %p
            In the point-particle limit, these non-geometric string vacua correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            that are defined purely algebraically, such as the non-geometric fiber spaces in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Connes-Lott+model"} Connes-Lott model
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+2d+CFT"} rational 2d CFT
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner model
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+geometry"} non-commutative geometry
                (as in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Connes-Lott+models"} Connes-Lott models
          %h3#type_ii_superstring_vacua Type II superstring vacua
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+geometry"} type II geometry
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-folds"} T-folds
                %li
                  %p
                    backgrounds of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+branes"} exotic branes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+generalized+geometry"} exceptional generalized geometry
          %h3#ExamplesHeteroticString Heterotic string vacua
          %p
            Strictly speaking, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacua"} perturbative string theory vacua
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            are
            %em all
            non-geometric, even if the apparent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            is plain
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of two rather different chiral halves:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the holomorphic part, say, is one chiral half of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
                on 10d
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %li
              %p
                the antiholomorphic part is one chiral half of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
                on a 26d-dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                that is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
                on the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leech+lattice"} Leech lattice
          %p
            While the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of these two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebras"} super vertex operator algebras
            is again a consistent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            anymore, even if its two halves do arise in (two distinct!) sigma-models.
          %p
            Analogous statements hold for most
            = succeed "-constructions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+CFT"} rational CFT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacua"} perturbative string theory vacua
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            (notably
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+models"} WZW models
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacuum"} perturbative string theory vacuum
